WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
DNA polymerase can proofread while copying DNA. If it adds a wrong base,

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.000
its exonuclease activity removes the incorrect base from the three prime end, allowing

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.500
the correct base to be added.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:18.444
Mismatch repair happens after replication is complete. Proteins scan the new double helix

00:00:18.444 --> 00:00:23.389
for mismatched bases. Specialized enzymes remove the affected section and replace it with

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:28.333
the correct DNA nucleotides.

00:00:28.333 --> 00:00:33.500
UV light can make adjacent cytosines and thymines bond covalently, distorting the DNA.

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:38.667
Repair proteins recognize the damage, cut out the damaged section, replace the missing

00:00:38.667 --> 00:00:43.833
bases, and reseal the backbone.
